[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Network Emulation, Interception, and Mocking in Selenium"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Modern web applications rely heavily on asynchronous network requests (XHR and Fetch). Testing these applications often requires controlling network traffic to simulate various conditions like slow connections, offline states, or specific API responses. Selenium 4 introduces native support for the Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP), allowing developers to inspect, intercept, modify, and mock network traffic directly within their automated tests."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"To use network emulation features in Selenium, you need Selenium 4 or higher and a Chromium-based browser (like Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge). The core class responsible for interacting with DevTools is 'org.openqa.selenium.devtools.DevTools' in Java or equivalent bindings in Python and JavaScript."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Emulating Network Conditions"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can simulate poor network performance, such as 3G or 2G connections, by configuring latency, download throughput, and upload throughput. This helps verify how your application handles loading states and timeouts."},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"DevTools devTools = ((ChromeDriver) driver).getDevTools();
devTools.createSession();
devTools.send(Network.enable(Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty()));
devTools.send(Network.emulateNetworkConditions(
    false,
    100,
    50000,
    10000,
    Optional.of(ConnectionType.CELLULAR3G),
    Optional.empty(),
    Optional.empty(),
    Optional.empty()
));"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Intercepting and Mocking Network Responses"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Mocking allows you to intercept outgoing requests and return predefined responses without hitting the actual backend server. This is essential for isolated UI testing, running tests offline, or simulating rare server error codes like 500 or 503."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Enable the Network domain in the DevTools session."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Define URL patterns to intercept using 'RequestPattern'."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Add a listener to handle intercepted requests and fulfill them with mock data."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"devTools.send(Network.enable(Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty()));
devTools.send(Network.setRequestInterception(List.of(
    new RequestPattern(Optional.of("*/api/data"), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty())
));

devTools.addListener(Network.requestIntercepted(), intercepted -> {
    if (intercepted.getRequest().getUrl().contains("api/data")) {
        String mockJsonResponse = "{\"status\": \"success\", \"data\": [\"Mock Item 1\", \"Mock Item 2\"]}";
        devTools.send(Network.continueInterceptedRequest(
            intercepted.getInterceptionId(),
            Optional.empty(),
            Optional.of("200 OK"),
            Optional.empty(),
            Optional.empty(),
            Optional.of(Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(mockJsonResponse.getBytes())),
            Optional.empty(),
            Optional.empty()
        ));
    } else {
        devTools.send(Network.continueInterceptedRequest(
            intercepted.getInterceptionId(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty(), Optional.empty()
        ));
    }
});"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always close the DevTools session or quit the driver after the test completes to free up system resources."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Keep mock payloads synchronized with your API contract specifications to prevent false positives in UI validation."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use specific URL matching patterns to avoid accidentally intercepting critical browser assets or analytics scripts."}]
